{"id": "EUVD-2026-101275", "enisaUuid": "edd2735d-9d54-3f40-9b8a-16d494ef6300", "description": "Turnpress through 0.4.2 contains an OS command injection vulnerability that allows attackers to execute shell commands by supplying .docx files with crafted names. The convertDocxToHtml function in src/converter.ts invokes pandoc through execa with shell:true, so shell metacharacters in the --docx path run with the victim's privileges during convert or create.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:17:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:20:08", "baseScore": 8.5, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jinghaihan/turnpress/pull/2", "https://github.com/jinghaihan/turnpress/blob/v0.4.2/src/converter.ts#L33-L61", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/turnpress-through-0.4.2-os-command-injection-via-crafted-docx-file-names"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110647", "GHSA-f273-crjh-xp28"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 1.04, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a29e1d9-cfa0-39ba-9beb-446d1815c709", "product": {"name": "turnpress", "vendor": {"name": "jinghaihan"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.4.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ec951af6-ff7a-3e88-83c5-d04c5b68027c", "vendor": {"name": "jinghaihan"}}], "isExploited": false}